@@ -22,7 +22,18 @@
 
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The non-Error rejection behaviour remains outside the scope of usage accounting in #93.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Turn usage — #93
+
+The chosen contract keeps one usage argument and sums provider calls, preserving the existing no-tool shape. A per-round breakdown is rejected for this change because it widens the API without being needed for turn billing; provider stop chunks retain their existing per-call usage. The hook signature must explicitly name its usage as a turn total. This requires a MINOR version bump and a changelog entry explaining that existing consumers record larger totals for tool turns.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once after the round loop and receives the sum of input, output and total tokens from every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer ([validated by: reports the sum of all three provider calls after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- Missing usage on any round contributes nothing to the sum; when no round reports usage, the hook receives undefined ([validated by: sums reported rounds across missing usage and preserves wholly absent usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- A turn with no tools preserves its existing response text and usage ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+- When both the running total and the incoming usage are defined, the accumulator sums each token field individually ([validated by: adds token counts from both usages when both are defined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L30)).
+- When the running total is undefined and a round reports usage, that usage becomes the new running total ([validated by: returns the defined usage when the accumulated total is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L36)).
+- When a round reports no usage and the running total is defined, the running total is unchanged ([validated by: returns the accumulated total when the incoming usage is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L41)).
+- When neither the running total nor the incoming usage is defined, the accumulator returns undefined ([validated by: returns undefined when both are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L46)).
